            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "VD711"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I do a slight variation on this recipe, which I learned from my 1/4 Lebanese roommate! First, \"gut\" the tomatoes before they are chopped so they don't have all those seeds and runny juices! Second, use red onion, and only 1/4 to 1/2 an onion depending on size. Third, in addition to the fresh-squeezed lemon, add a drizzle of extra virgin olive oil. And finally, I season with a dash of dried basil, kosher salt, pepper, and a generous sprinkle of dried (or fresh would be fine) parsley! Chill before serving. This dish is great with chicken and rice, or as a light lunch salad!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Arizona Desert Flower"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 2 roma tomatoes and 1 large cucumber (peeled). I removed the seeds from the cucumber and tomatoes, then sprinkled with salt to remove the excess moisture. I eyeballed the lemon juice and added a splash of garlic infused olive oil, a dash of dried italian seasoning and pepper as stated. I used 1/2 of a green onion (I prefer a lighter onion flavor). I let it sit overnight and ended up eating the ENTIRE thing for breakfast because I couldn't get enough of it. This will be made often--OUTSTANDING!",
            "datePublished": "2009-08-18T09:56:23.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "IrishTriplets"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my favorite salad. A friend made it for me and I went crazy over it! The only things I would change in this recipe is to add a 12 oz can(pitted) whole black olives - medium size. I keep them whole. Drain and rinse olives before adding to mix. I actually use the juice from 2 lemons and use about 1/2 cup or more of olive oil. For those who think the salad is bland... I'm guessing that you did not add enough salt &amp; pepper - please try it again - you will surprise yourself! It is fresh tasting and everyone goes nuts over it every time I make it. I usually chill it 30 minutes so the juices can marinate the veggies. I cannot wait to make this again!",
            "datePublished": "2008-04-28T19:37:15.847Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Carolyn Schwarte"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We loved the salad and it used our fresh garden vegetables. I did add a small amount of lemon flavored olive oil, garlic wine vinegar, and a dash of erythritol.",
            "datePublished": "2022-09-11T21:52:02.094Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christy Ratto-Bixby"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved this salad, great flavor, added thinly chopped spinach cause I had some on hand that I didn't want to spoil. It was so yummy!!! Will make this again and again!!",
            "datePublished": "2022-07-02T05:36:13.711Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Southern Belle"
            },
            "reviewBody": "YUM! I could live on these summer salads. This is so good, so easy. I used fresh lime juice because that’s what I prefer. sorry, I’m not about to “gut,“ my tomatoes. If I’m using store-bought tomatoes, that’s the only thing that makes them edible, and if I’m using homegrown tomatoes, I’m not wasting a speck of that flavor.For a different variation, next time I may chop celery into tiny pieces to add.",
            "datePublished": "2025-06-15T13:49:12.851Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Mary Palmquist Bixler"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used about 1/2c sweet onion, most of an English cucumber, and 2 tomatoes. I added 1 Tbsp of meyer lemon infused olive oil to the lemon juice, and topped with some parsley. It made a great summer salad, and was both easy and healthy. I may try adding a stalk of celery next time....",
            "datePublished": "2020-06-04T13:26:00.757Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "rascalgirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "A great recipe as is or to use as a starting point to match your favorite tastes. After reading other reviews, I added 1 T. each of garlic infused olive oil as well as Tuscan Herb olive oil, and 1/2 tsp dried Italian seasoning. Unfortunately, my lemon was far beyond any possible use and I resorted to using bottled lemon juice. The recipe was very forgiving and still tasted absolutely wonderful. I added the salt and pepper needed just prior to serving so as to give the other flavors a chance to blend first.",
            "datePublished": "2019-09-19T23:18:15.430Z"
          },
          {
